    "english":  "The northern wind brings the cold mist from the hills,\nmingling with the tears that fall like rain from my eyes.\nThe heavy clouds gather on the southern horizon,\npromising showers to drench the mountain fields where the millet ripens.\nThe wild jasmine vines, cut by the hill-dwellers\u0027 axes,\nsprout anew and climb around the hard-hearted sandalwood tree.\nIn this winter season of early frost, when lovers cling close,\nmy messenger tears have pleaded with him not to part;\nhow then could you, my heart, endure his absence\nin this cold land where even the stones seem to shiver?",
